  'Mathematics Unit Topic',
  'The altitude of a right-angled triangle is 7 cm less than its base. If the hypotenuse is
13 cm, find the lengths of the other two sides.',
  'Let base = x cm. Altitude = (x−7) cm. Hypotenuse = 13 cm.
By Pythagoras Theorem:
x2+(x−7)2 = 132
x2+x2−14x+49 = 169 =⇒ 2x2−14x−120 = 0
x2−7x−60 = 0
Factoring:
(x−12)(x+5) = 0 =⇒ x = 12 (since x > 0)
Base = 12 cm, Altitude = 12−7 = 5 cm.',
