) VALUES (
  'english-pdf-predicted-2',
  'english',
  'english-predicted',
  'PDF predicted question bank',
  'Q2. Short Story Writing from Outline [4 Marks]
Prompt: Write a readable story in about 100 words using the given outline: A cap-seller rests under a tree...
falls asleep... monkeys come down... steal caps... cap-seller wakes up... finds caps missing... throws his own
cap in frustration... monkeys copy him... throws caps down... collects caps and goes away. Give a suitable title
and moral.',
  'Title: The Clever Cap-Seller and the Monkeys',
  'Title: The Clever Cap-Seller and the Monkeys
Once a cap-seller was going to a market to sell his colorful caps. Exhausted by the afternoon heat, he sat under a
large banyan tree and fell asleep. A group of playful monkeys lived on the tree. Seeing the bag, they crept down,
opened it, took the caps, and put them on their heads.
When the cap-seller woke up, he was shocked to find his bag empty. Looking up, he saw the monkeys wearing his
caps. He tried shouting and gesturing, but the monkeys merely mimicked his actions. Remembering that monkeys
are imitators, he took off his own cap and threw it forcefully to the ground. The monkeys immediately threw down all
their caps. He quickly collected them and went happily on his way.
Moral: Wisdom and presence of mind can solve difficult problems.',
  '[]'::jsonb,
  NULL,
  'short_answer',
  4,
  'hard',
  'must_do',
