) VALUES (
  'science-pdf-predicted-19',
  'science',
  'science-predicted',
  'PDF predicted question bank',
  'Q19. [4 Marks] Esterification & Saponification Reactions:
(a) What is an esterification reaction? Write the chemical equation for the reaction
between ethanoic acid and ethanol in the presence of concentrated H2SO4.
(b) Define Saponification and write its balanced chemical reaction.
(c) Explain the micelle formation structure during the cleansing action of soap.',
  'ns:',
  'Ans:
(a) Esterification: Reaction between a carboxylic acid and an alcohol in the presence of an acid catalyst to
produce a sweet-smelling compound called an ester.
• Equation: CH3COOH (Ethanoic Acid) + C2H5OH (Ethanol) --(Conc. H2SO4)--> CH3COOC2H5 (Ethyl Ethanoate
Ester) + H2O
(b) Saponification: Alkaline hydrolysis of an ester using a base (NaOH) to regenerate alcohol and the sodium
salt of carboxylic acid (soap).
• Equation: CH3COOC2H5 + NaOH -> CH3COONa (Soap) + C2H5OH
(c) Micelle Cleansing Mechanism: A soap molecule consists of two ends: a hydrophilic ionic head (-COONa+)
that interacts with water and a hydrophobic hydrocarbon tail that attracts oil/dirt. In water, soap molecules align
radially into spherical clusters called micelles with hydrophobic tails buried inside trapping dirt and ionic heads
facing outward.',
  '[]'::jsonb,
  NULL,
  'short_answer',
  4,
  'hard',
