  'science',
  'science-predicted',
  'PDF predicted question bank',
  'Q20. [3 Marks] Double Fertilization in Flowering Plants:
(a) Draw a neat labeled diagram of a germinating pollen grain on a flower stigma.
(b) Explain Syngamy and Triple Fusion.
(c) State what the Ovule and Ovary develop into after fertilization.',
  'ns:',
  'Ans:
(a) Process: Pollen grain lands on sticky stigma -> Germinates and produces a pollen tube -> Pollen tube
carries 2 male gametes down the style to the ovule inside the ovary.
(b) Double Fertilization Components:
• Syngamy: One male gamete fuses with the female egg cell to form a diploid Zygote (2n), which develops into
the Embryo.
• Triple Fusion: Second male gamete fuses with 2 polar nuclei to form triploid Endosperm (3n), which provides
nourishment to developing embryo.
(c) Post-Fertilization Fate:
• Ovule matures into a Seed.
• Ovary wall ripens and develops into a Fruit.',
  '[]'::jsonb,
