  'science',
  'science-predicted',
  'PDF predicted question bank',
  'Q21. [3 Marks] Human Female Reproductive System & Contraception:
(a) Name the site of egg production, site of fertilization, and site of embryo implantation
in human females.
(b) Explain why menstruation occurs in human females.
(c) Compare Barrier Methods (Condoms) vs Surgical Methods (Vasectomy/Tubectomy) of
contraception.',
  'ns:',
  'Ans:
(a) Anatomical Locations: Site of egg production = Ovary; Site of fertilization = Fallopian Tube (Oviduct); Site
of embryo implantation = Uterus.
(b) Menstruation Mechanism: Every month, an ovary releases one egg and the uterus prepares its inner
spongy lining (endometrium) to receive a fertilized embryo. If fertilization does not occur, the egg dies and the
thick uterine lining breaks down, exiting through the vagina as blood and tissue flow lasting 2–8 days.
(c) Contraception Comparison:
• Barrier Method (Condom): Creates physical barrier preventing sperm entry. Only method that prevents
Sexually Transmitted Diseases (STDs).
• Surgical Method: Permanent blocking of gamete passages (Vasectomy in males by cutting Vas Deferens;
Tubectomy in females by cutting Fallopian Tubes).
