  'science-predicted',
  'PDF predicted question bank',
  'Q22. [3 Marks] Refractive Vision Defects & Optical Correction:
(a) What is Myopia (Near-sightedness)? State its two anatomical causes.
(b) Name the corrective lens used for Myopia and draw a ray diagram illustrating
correction.
(c) What is Hypermetropia and which lens corrects it?',
  'ns:',
  'Ans:
(a) Myopia: Vision defect where a person can see nearby objects clearly but cannot focus on distant objects.
Image of distant object forms in front of the retina.
• Two Causes: (1) Excessive curvature/thickness of eye lens. (2) Elongation of the eyeball.
(b) Myopia Correction: Corrected using a Concave Lens (Diverging Lens) of negative power (P < 0) that
diverges parallel rays so they focus sharply on the retina.
(c) Hypermetropia: Far-sightedness where distant vision is clear but nearby objects focus behind the retina.
Corrected using a Convex Lens (Converging Lens).
SECTION E: HIGH-YIELD STEP-BY-STEP NUMERICAL PROBLEMS (3 Marks
Each)',
