) VALUES (
  'science-pdf-predicted-23',
  'science',
  'science-predicted',
  'PDF predicted question bank',
  'Q23. [Optics Concave Mirror Numerical]
An object 4.0 cm in height is placed at 25.0 cm in front of a concave mirror of focal length
15.0 cm. Find the distance from the mirror at which a screen should be placed to obtain a
sharp image. Determine the nature and height of the image.
Step-by-Step Solution:
• Given values (by New Cartesian Sign Convention):
- Object height, h = +4.0 cm
- Object distance, u = -25.0 cm
- Focal length of concave mirror, f = -15.0 cm
• Using Mirror Formula: 1/f = 1/v + 1/u => 1/v = 1/f - 1/u
- 1/v = 1/(-15) - 1/(-25) = -1/15 + 1/25
- Taking LCM of 15 and 25 (75): 1/v = (-5 + 3)/75 = -2/75
- Image Distance, v = -75/2 = -37.5 cm
- Conclusion: Screen should be placed at 37.5 cm in front of the mirror.
• Calculating Image Height (h''):
- Magnification, m = -v/u = h''/h => h'' = -h * (v/u)
- h'' = -4.0 * [(-37.5) / (-25.0)] = -4.0 * 1.5 = -6.0 cm
• Nature of Image: The image is Real, Inverted, and Magnified (6.0 cm long).',
  'See the source predicted-question solution.',
