  'science-pdf-predicted-24',
  'science',
  'science-predicted',
  'PDF predicted question bank',
  'Q24. [Lens Formula & Power Numerical]
A concave lens has a focal length of 15 cm. At what distance should an object from the
lens be placed so that it forms an image at 10 cm from the lens? Also find the power of
the lens.
Step-by-Step Solution:
• Given values (Concave lens):
- Focal length, f = -15 cm
- Virtual image distance, v = -10 cm
• Using Lens Formula: 1/f = 1/v - 1/u => 1/u = 1/v - 1/f
- 1/u = 1/(-10) - 1/(-15) = -1/10 + 1/15
- Taking LCM of 10 and 15 (30): 1/u = (-3 + 2)/30 = -1/30
- Object Distance, u = -30 cm
- Conclusion: Object must be placed at 30 cm in front of the lens.
• Calculating Optical Power (P):
- f in meters = -15/100 = -0.15 m
- Power, P = 1 / f(m) = 1 / (-0.15 m) = -100/15 = -6.67 Dioptres (-6.67 D).
