  'social-science-pdf-predicted-22',
  'social-science',
  'social-science-predicted',
  'PDF predicted question bank',
  'Q22. [Economics - 4 Marks] Compare Formal and Informal sources of credit in India. Why is
it necessary to expand formal credit in rural areas?
OR
Q22 (OR). Explain the credit function of Self-Help Groups (SHGs) for the rural poor, particularly
women.',
  'Main Q: 1. Formal Credit: Provided by Banks and Cooperatives; supervised by RBI; low interest rates; clear',
  'Main Q: 1. Formal Credit: Provided by Banks and Cooperatives; supervised by RBI; low interest rates; clear
documentation and collateral required. 2. Informal Credit: Provided by Moneylenders, Traders, Relatives;
unsupervised; exorbitantly high interest rates leading to debt traps. 3. Need for Expansion: Rural poor rely
heavily (85%) on informal credit due to lack of collateral, driving them into debt cycles. 4. Economic
Growth: Cheap and accessible formal credit is crucial for agricultural inputs, small enterprises, and overall
poverty reduction. [1 + 1 + 1 + 1 = 4 Marks]
OR Q: 1. Structure: 15–20 members (usually neighborhood women) meet and save regularly
(₹25–100/month). 2. Small Internal Loans: Members take small low-interest loans from group savings for
emergency needs without collateral. 3. Bank Linkage: After 1–2 years of regular savings, the SHG becomes
eligible for bank loans in the name of the group for micro-enterprises. 4. Empowerment: Helps women
become financially self-reliant and provides a periodic platform to discuss social issues (health, domestic
violence). [1 + 1 + 1 + 1 = 4 Marks]
